            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 31-year-old male, admitted on 08/08/2024 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically and diagnostically consistent with acute appendicitis. Laboratory workup revealed elevated inflammatory markers, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed the diagnosis. The patient underwent a laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on the same day without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, he received intravenous fluids, analgesics, and prophylactic antibiotics. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. Wound healing was satisfactory, and the patient was mobilized early. He was discharged on 09/08/2024 in good general condition with oral analgesia and wound care instructions. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and pathology results review.</div>"
            },
